ial plexopathy from repetitive strain (possible but alarm signs suggest higher concern for neoplastic/vascular causes)", "Vitamin B12 deficiency (steroid/alcohol use creates risk but doesn't explain focal pattern)", "Thoracic outlet syndrome (bodybuilding context suggests possibility but alarm signs elevate cancer concern)"], "alarm_features": ["Subacute unilateral neurological deficit", "Significant weight loss (17 lbs in 1 month)", "Heavy smoking history (2 packs/day since age 25)", "Anabolic steroid use (neurotoxicity risk)", "Hypertension and diabetes (vascular risk factors)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Neoplastic Disease", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.5570484169626058, "posterior": 0.21329550679134934, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Absence of pathognomonic features for neoplastic disease maintains moderate support for this branch."], "evidence_against": ["The focal neurological pattern provides weak support for brachial plexopathy and weak exclusionary evidence against neoplastic disease."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Vascular Disease", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.34064792981946607, "posterior": 0.14575506915508077, "danger": 0.6, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["The patient's subacute neurological deficit with constitutional symptoms (weight loss, heavy smoking) provides moderate support for metastatic neoplasm and par…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_r